gh Split Ticket and the Economist rate it a Tossup, and prediction markets give the Democrat about a 29% chance.\n\nThe race's defining feature is the late-September ethics complaint alleging Boebert had relationships with staffers and made hush-money payments, which she denies as politically motivated. Challenger Eileen Laubacher has dramatically out-raised the incumbent, over $10 million to about $1 million, and holds a large cash advantage heading into the final stretch. With no public general-election polling, uncertainty is high, but the combination of district lean and incumbency keeps Boebert favored despite the scandal and money gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}]}